The issue is that the task function is enqueued. If the signal is aborted while the task is still in the queue (not yet running), the abort event is never checked. The current logic only checks `options.signal?.throwIfAborted();` *inside* the enqueued function, which is only called when the task is dequeued for execution.

Looking at the comment in the options.ts file:
> [`AbortSignal`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortSignal) for cancellation of the operation. When aborted, it will be removed from the queue and the `queue.add()` call will reject with an `AbortError`. If the operation is already running, the signal will need to be handled by the operation itself.

So according to the documentation, the signal abort should:
